@startuml
title UC09 — Publish Schematic (Activity Diagram · PlantUML Beta syntax)
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam nodesep 30
skinparam ranksep 45

' Swimlanes: Author, Frontend, Backend, Storage (S3),
' Litematica Parser Service, Database (per lab4/spec.md)

|Author|
start
: Open the publication creation page;

|Frontend|
: Send rights-check request to Backend;
|Backend|
: Validate authentication session (access token);
if (Session invalid?) then
  : Attempt refresh-token rotation (Database Session table · ADR-0007);
  if (Refresh succeeded?) then
    : Issue new access token; session now valid;
  else
    : Return 403 Forbidden;
    |Frontend|
    : Block form; offer Microsoft OAuth;
    stop
  endif
endif
: Check Author flag (isAuthor);
if (isAuthor = true?) then
  : Return 200 OK;
  |Frontend|
  : Display upload form;
else
  : Return 403 Forbidden;
  |Frontend|
  : Block form; offer Microsoft OAuth;
  stop
endif

|Author|
: Fill metadata (title, description, category, tags, supported game versions);
: Choose .litematica file and optionally .zip world archive;
: Click Publish;
|Frontend|
: Set validation_attempts = 0;
: Client-side validation (file extensions + required fields; .zip only if present);
if (Client validation failed?) then
  : Increment validation_attempts; display form errors;
  if (validation_attempts < 5?) then
    : Return to metadata form fill (bounded retry · Q4);
  else
    stop
  endif
else
  : Send POST /api/schematics (multipart/form-data) to Backend;
  |Backend|
  : Validate MIME type, size limits, classification links;
  if (Server validation failed?) then
    : Return 400 Bad Request;
    |Frontend|
    : Display error message;
    stop
  else
    : Generate slug; create DB draft (is_published = false);
    |Database|
    : Insert draft record;
    |Backend|
    : Fork parallel processing (Branch A Storage + Branch B Parser);
    fork
      |Backend|
      : Branch A — Upload .litematica + optional .zip to Storage (S3)
          [Q3: retry upload up to 5×, backoff 5s ×2ⁿ; on exhaustion → Branch A failed];
      |Storage (S3)|
      if (S3 upload succeeded?) then
        : Store objects; return schematic_url, world_zip_url (NULL if no zip);
        : Mark Branch A succeeded;
      else
        : Mark Branch A failed;
      endif
    fork again
      |Backend|
      : Branch B — Send .litematica binary to Litematica Parser Service;
      |Litematica Parser Service|
      : Parse NBT; verify checksums; extract dimensions (X,Y,Z),
          block count and materials list;
      if (Parser error — corrupted NBT / invalid structure?) then
        : Mark Branch B failed;
      else
        : Return JSON metadata;
        : Mark Branch B succeeded;
      endif
    end fork
    |Backend|
    : Join — synchronize both branches (every branch terminates → no deadlock);
    if (Either branch failed?) then
      : Q1=A — fail-fast: cancel any in-flight sibling branch;
      |Storage (S3)|
      : Delete uploaded objects (rollback);
      |Database|
      : Delete draft record;
      |Backend|
      : Return 422 Unprocessable Entity;
      |Frontend|
      : Display error message;
      stop
    else
      : Parser result valid;
      |Database|
      : Write schematic_url, world_zip_url, dimensions, block count, materials;
      : Set is_published = true; commit transaction;
      |Backend|
      : Return 201 Created + publication data;
      |Frontend|
      : Redirect Author to schematic view page (UC05);
      stop
    endif
  endif
endif
@enduml
